// The settle loop as it crossed a hooks module (observe-the-settle-run-live
// task 1.1): one general-purpose Agent-tool spawn made with `model` and `effort`
// parameters and its `turn.step` and `turn.complete`, captured on Claude Code
// 2.1.310 through scripts/host-probe.mjs, and the Bash results of the PR #25
// settle pass (2026-10-26) the kit replays: a `review ... --out --json`
// record, a `remediate-brief --json` answer, a `fixer-result` line, a
// `remediate-brief` STOP exit (an errored result whose text carries the
// stderr line), a `merge-confidence --json` answer and a `pipeline` text line.
//
// What the probe showed, so no test assumes otherwise: the spawn's `model` is
// the alias the call named (`sonnet`) while the result's `model` and the
// step's `usage.model` are the id (`claude-sonnet-5-5`); the spawn event has
// no effort field, the step's `effort` is the one the call named; the engine
// folds stderr into the result (an errored one reads `Error: Exit code N` and
// then the output) and trims the trailing newline.
//
// An importable module rather than JSON because `claude plugin test` runs the
// mod's tests with no filesystem. The scrubbed captures are the JSON files
// beside this one; test/spine/mod-pins.test.mjs pins that the two are the same.

